d 'LUSINFOSCORE': module to compute information score for free-text point-of-care lung ultrasound (LUS) reports
d
d    lusinfoscore reads free-text point-of-care lung ultrasound
d reports and assigns each report an information score. The score  
d  measures how much clinically useful information a report
d contains, using the items and point values of Table 1 (B-lines,  
d  sub-zones, pleural abnormalities, consolidation and air
d bronchograms, pleural effusion, laterality, localization,
d etiology or	 differential diagnosis, and cardiac findings).
d Higher scores mean more documented findings and more detail about
d them. It is not    a measure of disease severity. 
d
d KW: textual analysis
d KW: ultrasound reports
d
d Requires: Stata version 14
d
d Distribution-Date: 20261104
d
d Author:  Paul Walsh ,  Sutter Health Research Institute
d Support: email  yousentwhohome@@gmail.com
d
f lusinfoscore.ado
f lusinfoscore.sthlp
